# dyn.md D-18: a `COPY` demand on a key whose shared definition is
# `STV_PROTECTED` is refused by name, `copy-relocation-against-protected`:
# a copy would give the program its own `pv` while `libprot.so` keeps
# reading its protected one in place (gABI "Symbol Visibility":
# `STV_PROTECTED` is not preemptable). `main` prints `pv` and the
# library's `get_pv()`. All three references refuse the copy
# (E-shlib 5.6b): GNU ld ``copy relocation against non-copyable protected
# symbol `pv'``, lld `cannot preempt symbol: pv`, mold `cannot create a
# copy relocation for protected symbol 'pv'`.
#
# `-no-pie` code (`-fno-pie`, absolute or PC-relative access) needs a
# copy on both architectures. `-fPIE` code reaches `pv` through the GOT on
# AArch64 and needs no copy: it links and prints `9 9` (5.6a); on x86-64
# GCC's `-fPIE` reads extern data PC-relatively, which needs a copy in a
# PIE too, and it is refused.
#@ spec: dyn.md "D-18"
#@ arch: aarch64 x86_64
#@ fixture: shlib-prot

cc -O1 -fno-pie pv.c -o pv-nopie.o
cc -O1 -fPIE pv.c -o pv-pie.o
link gcc -no-pie pv-nopie.o -L. -lprot -o nopie
  exit: fail
  diag(bfd): copy relocation against non-copyable protected symbol `pv'
  diag(lld): cannot preempt symbol: pv
  diag(mold): cannot create a copy relocation for protected symbol 'pv'
  diag(mortar): copy relocation against non-copyable protected symbol `pv' in *
link(aarch64) gcc -pie pv-pie.o -L. -lprot -o pie
run(aarch64) pie
  stdout: 9 9
check(aarch64) readelf -rW pie
  not: R_AARCH64_COPY
link(x86_64) gcc -pie pv-pie.o -L. -lprot -o pie
  exit: fail
  diag(bfd): copy relocation against non-copyable protected symbol `pv'
  diag(lld): cannot preempt symbol: pv
  diag(mold): cannot create a copy relocation for protected symbol 'pv'
  diag(mortar): copy relocation against non-copyable protected symbol `pv' in *

#--- pv.c
#include <stdio.h>
#include "prot.h"

int main(void) {
  printf("%d %d\n", pv, get_pv());
  return 0;
}
